\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Blind-test NRMSE reduction relative to Plain Delta (mean and paired 95\% confidence interval; 16 seeds; each panel has its own labeled vertical scale). On the controlled spatial field, query-derived traces improve concentrated-query recall while the matched write trace does not; their distinction disappears under uniform queries. On WikiText-2, contiguous held-out queries give \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {QD}^{3}}\ a 2.62\% reduction, whereas \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {QD}^{3}}\ and Write Trace are nearly identical under uniform queries. Lower NRMSE is better.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:main-results}{{2}{11}{Blind-test NRMSE reduction relative to Plain Delta (mean and paired 95\% confidence interval; 16 seeds; each panel has its own labeled vertical scale). On the controlled spatial field, query-derived traces improve concentrated-query recall while the matched write trace does not; their distinction disappears under uniform queries. On WikiText-2, contiguous held-out queries give \QDDD \ a 2.62\% reduction, whereas \QDDD \ and Write Trace are nearly identical under uniform queries. Lower NRMSE is better}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {6.2}Where the gain comes from}{11}{subsection.6.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Mechanism tests on blind seeds. (a) The additional NRMSE reduction of \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {QD}^{3}}\ over the estimator- and capacity-matched Write Trace grows with the query-frequency exponent and begins near zero for uniform queries. (b) A small adaptive query subspace recovers the full online second-moment result; optimal rank is task dependent and selected only on validation seeds.}}{12}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{3}{12}{Mechanism tests on blind seeds. (a) The additional NRMSE reduction of \QDDD \ over the estimator- and capacity-matched Write Trace grows with the query-frequency exponent and begins near zero for uniform queries. (b) A small adaptive query subspace recovers the full online second-moment result; optimal rank is task dependent and selected only on validation seeds}{figure.3}{}}
